---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Get from '../components/Get.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Guide
  page="install"
  lede="Cupola is free, needs no account, and talks straight to the services you already run. Pick your device below; the first launch walks you through your services."
  questions={pick('account', 'away', 'certs', 'desktop')}
  related={['services', 'privacy', 'faq']}
  get={false}
>
  <div class="not-prose">
    <Get />
  </div>

  <h2 id="before">Before you start</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your own services.</strong> At least one of the <a href="/services/">eighteen</a>. Cupola does not include any.</li>
    <li><strong>Each one's address and login.</strong> Most use an API key: <a href="/services/">each service's page</a> says where to find it.</li>
    <li><strong>A way to reach them.</strong> Your home network is enough. Away from home, use your VPN or a reverse proxy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ios">iPhone and iPad</h2>
  {site.downloads.testflight ? (
    <p>Cupola is a public beta on TestFlight, Apple's app for testing. Install TestFlight from the App Store, open the <a href={site.downloads.testflight} rel="noopener">invitation link</a> on your iPhone or iPad, and tap <strong>Install</strong>. Updates arrive on their own.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>Cupola is coming to iPhone and iPad as a public TestFlight beta. It is not open yet: <a href={site.watch} rel="noopener">watch releases</a> to hear when it is.</p>
  )}
  {site.downloads.ipa && (
    <p>Prefer to sideload? <a href={site.downloads.ipa} rel="noopener">Download the unsigned <code>.ipa</code></a> and install it with AltStore, SideStore or Sideloadly. With a free Apple ID the install lasts seven days and has to be refreshed, and the widgets may stay empty. TestFlight is the way we recommend.</p>
  )}

  <h2 id="android">Android</h2>
  {site.downloads.apk ? (
    <p><a href={site.downloads.apk} rel="noopener">Download the <code>.apk</code></a> and open it. Android asks once to allow installs from your browser. New versions install over the old one. To have them arrive on their own, add <code>{site.repo.replace('https://', '')}</code> to Obtainium.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>The Android <code>.apk</code> comes with the first release on GitHub. It is not out yet: <a href={site.watch} rel="noopener">watch releases</a> to hear when it is.</p>
  )}

  <h2 id="mac">Mac</h2>
  {site.downloads.testflight && (
    <p>The Mac app is in the same beta. Open the <a href={site.downloads.testflight} rel="noopener">invitation link</a> on your Mac and install it from TestFlight.</p>
  )}
  {site.downloads.macos ? (
    <p>{site.downloads.testflight ? 'Or skip TestFlight: ' : ''}<a href={site.downloads.macos} rel="noopener">download the <code>.dmg</code></a> (Apple silicon) and drag Cupola to Applications. It is signed and notarized by Apple, so it opens like any other app.</p>
  ) : !site.downloads.testflight && (
    <p>The Mac app is coming as a TestFlight beta and a signed <code>.dmg</code>. Neither is open yet: <a href={site.watch} rel="noopener">watch releases</a> to hear when it is.</p>
  )}

  <h2 id="windows-linux">Windows and Linux</h2>
  {site.downloads.windows && site.downloads.linux ? (
    <p>Every <a href={site.releases} rel="noopener">release</a> includes a build for <a href={site.downloads.windows} rel="noopener">Windows</a> and one for <a href={site.downloads.linux} rel="noopener">Linux</a>, both x64. On Windows, unzip and run <code>cupola.exe</code> (SmartScreen asks once, as the build is unsigned). On Linux, untar and run <code>cupola</code>; it needs GTK 3 and libsecret. Neither is tested on a real machine yet, so tell us how it goes.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>Windows and Linux builds come with the first release on GitHub. Until then, <a href="#source">build Cupola from source</a>.</p>
  )}

  <h2 id="source">From source</h2>
  <p>Cupola is a Flutter app. With the Flutter SDK named in <code>pubspec.yaml</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone {site.repo}.git
cd {site.repo.split('/').pop()}
flutter pub get
flutter run</code></pre>

  <h2 id="first-run">The first run</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>One service at a time.</strong> Add what you run and skip the rest. Test each connection before saving: if it fails, Cupola says why.</li>
    <li><strong>Home and away.</strong> Give a connection a second address for when you are out.</li>
    <li><strong>A second device in one code.</strong> <strong>Settings › Security › Set up another device</strong> copies everything to a new phone, encrypted, over your Wi-Fi.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>

<style>
  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--r-button);
    background: rgb(18 18 24 / 0.9);
    border: 1px solid var(--hair);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  pre code {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .not-prose {
    max-width: none;
    width: min(var(--well), calc(100vw - 2 * var(--gutter)));
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
</style>
